cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "STUR: Measurement and Gravity from the Quantum Level Up"
abstract: >-
  One equation for the double slit, measurement and gravity, derived from
  quantum fields. Branch i of a superposition carries its own field states,
  including gravity's TEGR tetrad; interference is weighted by the record
  overlap and phases by the action difference. The Born rule is derived, G
  follows from vacuum entanglement, and general relativity's classic tests are
  recovered. A Markovian statistical gravity smeared at the entanglement cutoff
  would heat matter 6e10 times faster than the Earth's heat flow, so under that
  identification gravity's field follows each branch: two diamonds held in
  superposition become entangled with phase 2.19 rad, as perturbative quantum
  gravity also predicts. Oppenheim's classical gravity is bounded by a
  shape-free one-particle inequality, a worked example within existing work
  rather than a new result. Every number is reproduced by the
  scripts in src/.
authors:
